==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Glowstick Guys]] spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[MikuDoge]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*2 [[MikuGory|MikuGories]] spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Sakura Miku (Enemy)|Sakura Miku]] spawns as the boss.
**15 [[MikuDoge]]s spawn, delay 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
**15 [[MikuDoge]]s spawn, delay 1~2 seconds<sup>30f~60f</sup>.
**2 [[MikuGory|MikuGories]] spawn, delay 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
**4 [[MikuGory|MikuGories]] spawn, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
**2 [[MikuBear]]s spawn, delay 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
**1 [[Hatsune Miku (Enemy)|Hatsune Miku]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Tanky high damage units with relatively short attack animations and short range make this level much easier. [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] is one such example.

==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 11.5 Update|version 11.5]], the first group of MikuDoges had a spawn pattern of 10~6.7 seconds instead of just 10. It didn't work properly because the maximum time was lower than the minimum, so in practice nothing changed.

